{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Ce4mULxb5TUPBzntF4Gxv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Placement decision:**\n\nI would add the new rule to **§2, Failure handling**, as a third bullet (or fold it into the existing \"Timeouts are explicit\" bullet). Here's the edited region:\n\n```markdown\n## 2. Failure handling\n\n- **Retries are bounded and jittered.** Every retry wrapper declares\n  its maximum attempt count at the call site; backoff is exponential\n  with jitter, and a non-retriable error class aborts immediately —\n  enumerate those classes beside the wrapper, not in a distant\n  constants file.\n- **Timeouts are explicit.** No call inherits a library default\n  timeout silently; the call site states its per-attempt timeout.\n  A retry wrapper must also cap total elapsed time at the call site,\n  not only attempt count — a per-attempt timeout with unbounded\n  attempts still hangs the caller.\n```\n\n**Rationale:** The new rule is a direct refinement of the existing \"Timeouts are explicit\" bullet, tightening the contract by requiring a *wall-clock cap alongside* the per-attempt timeout already mandated. It lives in the same failure-handling concern and addresses the same enforcement point (call site declaration), so it folds into that bullet as a clarifying second sentence rather than standing alone."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":645,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":294,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
